What Canageek was referring to (with the jellies/boulders) is a trick to 
make your character inaccessible to foes; if you are surrounded by blue 
jellies and each of the 8 of them have a boulder on top (an easy 
arrangement with two scrolls) then you have a fortress. You could also 
do something like fill a whole level with foes so no more can be created 
(gremlins and long worms come to mind..) and then just use normal 
boulders. Or have peaceful monsters and forget the boulders entirely. 
Once in there, I can think of two methods of everlasting nutrition:

1. Ring of slow digestion and praying. Even in the worst possible case 
of prayer timeout, you will always be able to pray by the time you go 
from 1000 to 0 hunger with a ring of slow digest.

2. Two rings of slow digestion, taking each one off before the specific 
turn checks it for the hunger point. Each ring is 1 hunger per 20 turns, 
but they're checked on something like the 5th and 15th turn in each 20 
turn cycle, so if you take the correct one off and put it back on, you 
can have them always appear to be off. Obviosly this is insanely 
impractical in reality.


I suppose polymorphing yourself into yourself would work as well. A high 
INT wizard could cast the spell eternally. Do you get full nutrition for 
ANY polymorph, or just into yourself? Other possibilities to consider 
would be:
-A horn of plenty, the PYEC, and a ring of slow digest. Can you 
guarantee enough nutrition to go forever?
-Some setup with black puddings (do they always leave corpses?). If they 
don't always leave corpses then there's still the chance of going 
forever without something to eat. If they do, then with the right setup 
of damage and healing you could last forever even with all of the random 
factors.


